# Local first, publish only on approval

Work and review everything locally before anything reaches GitHub or Vercel. This saves Vercel build credits: every push to a connected repo and every deploy triggers a build.

## While working

1. Make the requested changes.
2. Verify them on the local Vite dev server (`npm run dev -- --host`, port 5173), so the user can also check on their phone over the LAN.
3. Commit locally with a concise message focused on why. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, secrets, or `node_modules`).
4. Do NOT `git push`, and do NOT run any `vercel` deploy (preview or production).

## Publishing (only after the user explicitly says OK)

1. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD` to review what will go out.
2. Push to `origin main` (use `git pull --rebase origin main` first if the push is rejected).
3. Deploy once to production: `npx vercel --prod --yes`.

